# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the prefill SDPA programme's oneq jobs (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a
# throwaway commit of the integration branch (a branch that carries optimisation/ttnn-op/sdpa_prefill_oneq) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. ONE TAG AT A TIME; wait for the run to
# finish; never cancel a running card job. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled in by whoever drives the
# window (@SERVED_IMAGE@: the served image's reference; @K64J_OQ_GRAFT_DIR@ and @K64J_OQ_TTNNCPP_SHA256@: the K64j-OQ graft directory and its binary's digest, the K64J_OQ_TTNNCPP_SHA256 line of
# L1). C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the window's own image (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env). ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the read rules and the minutes.
# L1 (the graft build, cardm, no device): build_k64j_oq.sh builds the K64j-OQ graft in the ttbuild container: K64j's exact source tree and patches (build_k64j.sh's staging, step for step) plus the ONE
# change of apply_factory_ps.py (flag 0x8 of the prefill SDPA program word: one q chunk per core). It never writes the K64j graft and never overwrites an existing K64j-OQ graft. Before it publishes anything
# it proves the result is K64j plus that change and nothing else: K64j alone, rebuilt in the same ttbuild, compared with the base binary (REPRODUCED = byte-identical, else a warning); every QWEN string of
# the base survives and the only new ones are the two oneq literals; the exported symbols are the base's; _ttnn.so and every op directory (the chain reader included) are the base's; the manifest differs
# from the base's in one line. Then ttbuild is restored and rebuilt.
# READ: 'K64J_OQ_TTNNCPP_SHA256=<sha>' and the line 'ok    REPRODUCED: K64j rebuilt alone ...' (the warning variant is acceptable only with the other checks green); the results hold the manifest, the
# QWEN-string and symbol lists and k64j-oq-build-summary.txt. The sha is the EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256 of every job below. STOP on any FAIL line. Duration (estimate): 20 min (about three ninja runs of 30 to 60 s).
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/sdpa_prefill_oneq/build_k64j_oq.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=
C2_CARDM_ENV=
